<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM load factor rises in September.</title>
<headline>KLM load factor rises in September.</headline>
<text>
<p>AMSTERDAM, Oct 7, Reuter - Provisional traffic and load factor figures from KLM Royal Dutch Airlines (millions of tonne-kilometres unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>			     Sept '96  Sept '95  Apr-Sep 96 Apr-Sep 95</p>
<p>TOTAL TRAFFIC</p>
<p>Traffic			 755.2     703.0     4,399.0    4,070.5</p>
<p>Capacity			966.3     944.5     5,986.3    5,551.6</p>
<p>Load factor (pct)	    75.8	74.4	  72.5	 73.3</p>
<p>PASSENGER TRAFFIC</p>
<p>Passenger kilometres    4,388.1   4,074.2    25,563.6   23,540.1</p>
<p>Seat kilometres</p>
<p>Load factor (pct)	    79.0	78.3	  76.8	 76.7</p>
<p>FREIGHT TRAFFIC</p>
<p>Traffic			 340.1     317.3     1,937.0    1,858.5</p>
<p>Capacity			488.0     469.6     2,976.0    2,782.7</p>
<p>Load factor (pct)	    69.7	67.6	  65.1	 66.8</p>
<p>KLM said that over the six-month period ending September 30 its overall load factor declined to 72.5 percent from 73.3 percent in the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>This reflected a seven percent increase in overall traffic in the six-month period and an eight percent increase in capacity.</p>
<p>Cargo traffic in the six-month period increased four percent and cargo capacity was up seven percent, while passenger traffic increased nine percent on a capacity increase of eight percent.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
